-- title:
--   Transitivity of diamond operators on pole-chart primes, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L((\mathsf q))/L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), that is, the subfield of the Laurent series field $L((\mathsf q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image (under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), induced by $\mathbb Q \to L$) of the rational $q$-expansion function field attached to $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction-of-units map out of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ given by the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'`. Let $A$ be a commutative ring with algebra structures on $L$ and on $K$ forming a scalar tower, and let $j \in K$ be an element whose image in $L((\mathsf q))$ is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= \mathsf q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral } j\text{-numerator series})$. Write $F_0 \subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ for [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull (q ^ 2 * M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansions `qExpand ℚ d jq` for $d \mid q^2M'$ (the floor), and $B$ for [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L144), the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$. The assertion is that there exist a type $G$ with a group structure, a finiteness structure, and a multiplicative semiring action of $G$ on $K$, such that: the action commutes with the $L$-scalar multiplication on $K$; every $g \in G$ fixes each $x \in K$ whose image in $L((\mathsf q))$ lies in $F_0$, and conversely every $x \in K$ fixed by all of $G$ has image in $F_0$; every $g$ fixes each element $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A\,K\,a$ and fixes $j$; $B$ is stable under $G$; and for all prime ideals $y, y'$ of $B$ such that $b \in y \iff b \in y'$ for every $b \in B$ whose image in $L((\mathsf q))$ lies in $F_0$, there exists $g \in G$ with: for all $b, b' \in B$ with $(b' : K) = g \cdot (b : K)$ one has $b \in y \iff b' \in y'$.
--
--   This is the transitivity of the diamond operators on the primes of the $\infty$-chart (pole chart) of the integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ lying over a given prime of the $X_0(q^2M')$ floor, in the case $q = 2$, together with the identification of the floor as the exact fixed field of the acting group. It feeds the verification that the localisations of this chart at such primes are regular local rings, in the analysis of the fibres of the covering $X_H(q^2M') \to X_0(q^2M')$ along the $\infty$-branch.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_mulSemiringAction_chartAlgInf_isPrime_conj_of_forall_mem_floor_iff_xH_of_eq_two.lean

